       ssttrruucctt mmaalllliinnffoo22 mmaalllliinnffoo22((vvooiidd));;

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  return  a  copy of a structure containing information
       about memory allocations performed by mmaalllloocc(3) and related  functions.
       The structure returned by each function contains the same fields.  How‐
       ever, the older function, mmaalllliinnffoo(), is deprecated since the type used
       for the fields is too small (see BUGS).

       Note  that not all allocations are visible to these functions; see BUGS
       and consider using mmaalllloocc__iinnffoo(3) instead.

       The _m_a_l_l_i_n_f_o_2 structure returned by mmaalllliinnffoo22() is defined as follows:

           struct mallinfo2 {
               size_t arena;     /* Non-mmapped space allocated (bytes) */
               size_t ordblks;   /* Number of free chunks */
               size_t smblks;    /* Number of free fastbin blocks */
               size_t hblks;     /* Number of mmapped regions */
               size_t hblkhd;    /* Space allocated in mmapped regions
                                    (bytes) */
               size_t usmblks;   /* See below */
               size_t fsmblks;   /* Space in freed fastbin blocks (bytes) */
               size_t uordblks;  /* Total allocated space (bytes) */
               size_t fordblks;  /* Total free space (bytes) */
               size_t keepcost;  /* Top-most, releasable space (bytes) */
           };

       The _m_a_l_l_i_n_f_o structure returned by the deprecated  mmaalllliinnffoo()  function
       is exactly the same, except that the fields are typed as _i_n_t.

       The structure fields contain the following information:

       _a_r_e_n_a     The  total  amount  of  memory  allocated by means other than
                 mmmmaapp(2) (i.e., memory allocated on the  heap).   This  figure
                 includes both in‐use blocks and blocks on the free list.

       _o_r_d_b_l_k_s   The number of ordinary (i.e., non‐fastbin) free blocks.

       _s_m_b_l_k_s    The number of fastbin free blocks (see mmaalllloopptt(3)).

       _h_b_l_k_s     The number of blocks currently allocated using mmmmaapp(2).  (See
                 the discussion of MM__MMMMAAPP__TTHHRREESSHHOOLLDD in mmaalllloopptt(3).)

       _h_b_l_k_h_d    The  number  of  bytes  in  blocks  currently allocated using
                 mmmmaapp(2).

       _u_s_m_b_l_k_s   This field is unused, and is always 0.  Historically, it  was
                 the "highwater mark" for allocated space—that is, the maximum
                 amount  of  space  that  was  ever allocated (in bytes); this
                 field was maintained only in nonthreading environments.

       _f_s_m_b_l_k_s   The total number of bytes in fastbin free blocks.

       _u_o_r_d_b_l_k_s  The total number of bytes used by in‐use allocations.

       _f_o_r_d_b_l_k_s  The total number of bytes in free blocks.

       _k_e_e_p_c_o_s_t  The total amount of releasable free space at the top  of  the
                 heap.  This is the maximum number of bytes that could ideally
                 (i.e.,  ignoring  page  alignment restrictions, and so on) be
                 released by mmaalllloocc__ttrriimm(3).

